        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T22:22:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like a good place to add a few words on the purpose of SDC files and how they work, including:\n\n1. There may be one SDC file accompanying each SDM file. An SDC file without a corresponding SDM file is garbage.\n2. They are always local on device.\n3. They are only read and written by the ART module, but may be read by a later version of it(?).\n\nIf #1 is correct then we should ensure that a newly written SDM file cannot pick up an older garbage SDC file. Somewhere in this CL stack that ought to pop up, but I don\u0027t know where yet. Just a note to self.\n\n#3 is important for file format stability considerations.",
      "revId": "ac0c568e04389babe94db101353cf829b617bf69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
